What is POM?

Page Object Model (POM) is a design pattern in test automation where:

Page locators are stored in page classes.
Page actions/methods are stored in page classes.
Test cases remain in test files.

This separates page logic from test logic.

Why Do We Use POM?

Without POM:

await page.locator('#user-name').fill('standard_user');
await page.locator('#password').fill('secret_sauce');
await page.locator('#login-button').click();

The same code gets repeated in many tests.

With POM:

await loginPage.login(
  'standard_user',
  'secret_sauce'
);

Code becomes cleaner and reusable.

Benefits of POM
1. Reusability

Write locators and methods once.

Use them in multiple tests.

2. Maintainability

If locator changes:

#login-button

to

#sign-in-button

Only update it in one place.

3. Readability

Tests become easy to understand.

Example:

await loginPage.login();

is easier to read than multiple locator actions.

4. Reduced Code Duplication

Same code is not repeated across tests.

Folder Structure
project
│
├── pages
│   └── LoginPage.ts
│
├── tests
