│
└── playwright.config.ts
What Goes Inside a Page Class?
Locators
readonly username: Locator;
readonly password: Locator;
readonly loginButton: Locator;
Methods
async login(username: string, password: string)

Methods perform actions on the page.

What Goes Inside a Test File?
Test Cases
test('Valid Login')
Assertions
expect(page).toHaveURL(/inventory/);
Basic POM Flow
Step 1

Create Page Class

export class LoginPage
Step 2

Store Locators

this.username = page.locator('#user-name');
Step 3

Create Methods

async login(username: string, password: string)
Step 4

Use Methods in Tests

await loginPage.login(
  'standard_user',
  'secret_sauce'
);
Constructor Purpose
constructor(page: Page) {
  this.page = page;
}

Purpose:

Receives Playwright page object.
Stores it inside the class.
Allows methods and locators to use the page.
